  "content": {
    "id": "p13-q13-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "If air resistance is neglected, the distance $d$ metres that an object falls from rest is directly proportional to the square of the time $t$ seconds of the fall. An object falls 9.6 m in 1.4 seconds. How far will the object fall in 2.8 seconds?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$38.4\\text{ m}$",
      "worked": "Since $d\\propto t^2$, write $d=kt^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}9.6 &= k(1.4)^2\\\\k &= \\frac{9.6}{(1.4)^2}\\\\d &= \\frac{9.6}{(1.4)^2}(2.8)^2\\\\d &= 9.6\\times 2^2\\\\d &= 38.4\\end{align*}$$\nThe object falls $38.4\\text{ m}$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 30
  },
